/-!
# The marked abelian span of the opposite involution

The cubic actor cycles the three distinct square involutions, so its three
cyclic factors exhaust the source conjugate family. The first two factors
are independent C4 groups. Replacing the third generator by their product w
exhibits the actual span as C4² × C2, since w lies outside the source plane.
The final source application constructs one triple and combines the span
model, nonfusion, omega identity and moved-plane conclusions on that triple.

The remaining core-centralizer geometry and global recognition remain with
qt-e-14322-core-collapse; no existence of LocalGeometry is asserted here.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith 14.3.22, printed p.999.
-/

public section
